# 基本図形編集のプロセスの縦書きの文字枠でかな漢字変換 (design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py: a
# figure of 30 small rectangles, two zigzag lines and one piece of text "ABC" written down the
# line (mkbig fig 30 4 1 1; its box from 100,120 to 140,240 of the figure, 210,247 to 250,367
# on the screen). With the desktop's figure editor and then with the one running as a
# process: the text pressed twice, the caret put at the end, かな typed after ひらがなカタカナ;
# what is being converted runs down the line from the caret, on white, each clause lined on
# its left, the caret a red bar across under it (the shots, and the
# pixels of the bar and of the letters); Space converts it, Escape takes the conversion back, Escape again
# ends the editing, and the figure is saved and closed.
# Keys: End 4D, ひらがなカタカナ 88, Space 2C, Esc 29, 英数 39; Ctrl+E 08 01.
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 30 4 1 1
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 500
dclick 228 260
sync 600
key 4D
key 88
text kana
sync 600
shot vime_kernel
pixel 232 320 D00000
pixel 246 320 D00000
pixelnot 240 300 FFFFFF
key 2c
wait 800
shot vime_kernel_conv
key 29
key 29
key 29
key 39
sync 600
key 16 01
sync 600
key 08 01
wait 1500
mkbig fig 30 4 1 1
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 33
wait 500
logmark
dclick 228 260
expectsince figure: text editing begun
key 4D
key 88
text kana
wait 500
shot vime_process
pixel 232 320 D00000
pixel 246 320 D00000
pixelnot 240 300 FFFFFF
key 2c
wait 800
shot vime_process_conv
key 29
key 29
key 29
key 39
wait 300
key 16 01
wait 500
key 08 01
wait 1500
